{"title":"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each day, Ella loaded her truck with red shirts and blue shirts for delivery to two stores. At Store 1, she dropped off some shirts, and at Store 2 she dropped off all remaining shirts.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On Tuesday, she loaded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> red shirts and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> blue shirts. At Store 1, she dropped of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the red shirts, and no blue shirts. What percentage of the shirts dropped off at Store 2 were blue?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because none of the blue shirts were dropped off to Store 1, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> blue shirts must have been dropped off to Store 2. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the red shirts were dropped off to Store 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/5158c98eda10cd217124a22a3a68d50dd6b8242c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\% - 40\\% = 60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"17\" /> of the red shirts must have been dropped off to Store 2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd7edd3842c40dbc1e54e522917a6e07b43c92e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the red shirts would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4fc2d9d469bc847a122b68cb14b7a6a3ad0779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\% \\times 5x = \\frac{3}{5} \\times 5x = 3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"38\" /> red shirts.\n</p><p>This means that the total number of shirts dropped off at Store 2 was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d6580941dc18adc3d16e0044e1ec5173128b5335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 5x = 8x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d19f9668800e9d3f9634f585c8431b302d5124d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5x}{8x} = \\frac{5}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" /> of the shirts dropped off at Store 2 were blue. As a percentage, this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8670e79ccd4613f97e6ca8631808a7c9ac94db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{8} \\times 100\\% = \\boxed{62.5\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"163\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018025731\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 49/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 263/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1953/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.996      1 2024_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    5.996      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35154:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018025731 and revision id 277858. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}